think The hu_moments log named three crux-first siblings: a CONTOUR/perimeter tracer (Moore-neighbor), a two-level MULTI-THRESHOLD, a SHAPE-MATCH distance over the Hu vectors; plus the round top-hat on a real photo (a fetch gate, surfaced not crossed). Lindy-first crux-first takes the CONTOUR tracer -- the most durable (a whole shape-descriptor family descends from an ordered boundary: perimeter, chain code, corners, polygon simplification) and the hardest-solvable-yet-tractable (an ordered boundary walk is a genuinely new capability nothing in the family yet provides -- every earlier reader returns an UNORDERED reduction).
think Studied label.rye (the LabelMap and its dense raster-ordered labels), centroid.rye (the compose-over-label pattern and witness shape), branch.rye (the eight-neighbor ring idiom and out-of-bounds-is-background rule), the README family bullets, a witness template. Built image/contour.rye composing over label: trace_contour walks a component's outer ring clockwise by Moore-neighbor tracing (start topmost-then-leftmost, sweep clockwise from just past the backtrack, stop on return to start), perimeter counts the ring, paint_contour renders it white on black round-tripping QOI.
think Designed the decisive crux before coding -- the OUTLINE-NOT-FILL fact no earlier reader can see: a solid 3x3 block (area 9) and the same block carved to a hollow ring (area 8) share the IDENTICAL outer contour point-for-point, so the outer boundary is blind to an interior hole, a different fact from the fill. Hand-traced the 3x3 and 5x5 Moore walks to fix exact perimeters (16 for a 5x5, 8 for a 3x3, 12 for a 4x4) and the interior-excluded claim before writing an assert.
obs Caught a real subtlety in my own fixtures before a byte: a Moore boundary walk visits a 1-pixel-wide shape TWICE (out and back), so a 1-tall 8-bar's ring length is 14, not its 8 pixels -- my first equal-area crux was wrong. Fixed it to two shapes thick enough that each ring pixel is visited once: a compact 4x4 block (area 16, perimeter 12, encloses a 2x2 interior) against a spread 2x8 block (area 16, perimeter 16, all boundary) -- equal area, different outline, the compactness area cannot express. Measurement beats memory: I traced the walk by hand rather than trusting the tidy count.
obs GREEN on the first full metal run, no algorithm reds. Fixed one stale claim in the GREEN print (the old 1-tall-bar line) to match the shape actually proven. TAME style bans clean, width-check exit 0, plain 7-bit ASCII, living-docs-lint GREEN, living-card-ascii GREEN.
